The '''Umbaran [[Militia]]''', also known as the '''Umbaran military''', was the defense force of the [[planet]] [[Umbara]] that became aligned with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] following the assassination of [[Senator]] [[Mee Deechi]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. Largely isolated from the rest of [[the galaxy]], the [[Umbaran]]s developed advanced and formidable technology for their [[Umbaran soldier|soldiers]], which they unleashed on the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] at the [[Battle of Umbara]].

==Description==
During the [[Clone Wars]], the Umbaran Militia defended their [[homeworld]] from the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]]. The soldiers were fierce fighters, who made clever use of [[Umbara]]'s advanced technology, which included a gas that increased reaction time, while it reduced fear when inhaled. As the Umbarans could see into the [[Ultraviolet]] spectrum, the Militia gained an advantage over the Republic's forces, while they fought amid their home [[planet]]'s shadows and gloom. Members of the Militia were effective at stealth, and were skilled in armed combat, infiltrations and military tactics.<ref name="Join the Battle">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Character Encyclopedia - Join the Battle!]]''</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Umbara was one of the major Separatist planets. The locals fought pretty hard, and got stomped pretty solidly.|Eli N. Vanto|audio=Vanto-Umbara.flac|<ref name="Thrawn">[[Thrawn (novel)|''Thrawn'']]</ref>}}
Following the assassination of [[Senator]] [[Mee Deechi]] of the [[Galactic Senate]] in [[21 BBY]], the planet Umbara seceded from the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> and joined the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. In response to this action, the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] was deployed to the planet to participate in an invasion that would later become known as the [[Battle of Umbara]]. While there, the Republic forces encountered fierce resistance from the local Umbaran Militia, who utilized extremely advanced and deadly technology in their defense of their homeworld.<ref name="Darkness" />

==Vehicles and machinery==
<div style="float:right">[[File:ShadowCrawler-SoPArtFeature.png|thumb|300px|right|An Impeding Assault Tank bursts from underground]]</div>
Umbaran vehicles were more technologically advanced than those developed by the Republic, with many utilizing touch-sensitive [[Hologram|holographic]] controls. Umbarans made use of [[Zenuas 33 Umbaran starfighter]]s<ref name="Darkness" /> and [[Umbaran support ship]]s<ref name="PoD" /> for aerial engagements, while ground combat vehicles included [[Umbaran mobile heavy cannon]]s, [[Impeding Assault Tank]]s,<ref name="General" /> and [[Umbaran hover tank]]s.<ref name="Darkness" />

==Weapons and equipment==
[[Umbaran soldier]]s of the Militia wore helmets that pumped gas within, which increased their reflexes and aggression in battle.<ref name="thegeneraltrivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-general-trivia|text="The General" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> They wielded [[Umbaran blaster pistol|blaster pistols]], planted [[mine]]s, and deployed [[Scutiger-100 stealth droid]]s to electrocute enemy soldiers.<ref name="Darkness" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Battle of Umbara gave the crew of [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''The Clone Wars'']] a chance to create a new unique military force. [[Kilian Plunkett]] described Umbara as a "video game planet," and said their military gave them opportunities for ideas that would not usually fit in the show's Republic or Separatist aesthetics. [[Dave Filoni]], who described the Umbaran aesthetic as "[[Wikipedia:Polyvinyl chloride|PVC plastic]]," said it would lend a very alien quality that would help distinguish them from the clone troopers.<ref name="DWoU">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season Four|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season Four]]</ref>

